    "problem_statement": "**Issue Text**\n\nChunkedUpdate.flush() doesn't update database correctly\n\nDescription\n\nWhen using ChunkedUpdate to batch update multiple records, the updates are not being applied correctly to the database. The queue is being sorted after the update_many operation is performed, which means the updates aren't being properly processed.\n\nConsider the following example:\n\n```python\ntbl = db['my_table']\ntbl.insert_many([\n    dict(temp=10, location='asdf'), \n    dict(temp=20, location='qwer'), \n    dict(temp=30, location='asdf')\n])\n\nchunked_tbl = chunked.ChunkedUpdate(tbl, 'id')\nchunked_tbl.update(dict(id=1, temp=50))\nchunked_tbl.update(dict(id=2, location='asdf'))\nchunked_tbl.update(dict(id=3, temp=50))\nchunked_tbl.flush()\n\n# Expected: records should be updated with new values\n# Actual: updates are not applied correctly\n```\n\nThe issue appears to be in the order of operations in the `flush()` method of the `ChunkedUpdate` class. The queue is being sorted after the database update operation, which means the updates aren't being properly processed."
  },
